							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;"><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">September 29, 2006, the US Senate agreed to the Military Commissions Act of 2006 which gives US President George Bush unprecedented power to detain and try people as part of their “War on Terror.” President Bush is then expected to sign the Act into law. Broadly, the new Act does 3 things:<br /><br />&nbsp; &nbsp;1. Strips the right of detainees to habeas corpus (the traditional right of detainees to challenge their detention);<br />&nbsp; &nbsp;2. Gives the US President the power to detain indefinitely anyone—US or foreign nationals, from within the US, and from abroad—it deems to have provided material support to anti-US hostilities, and even use secret and coerced evidence (i.e. through use of torture) to try detainees who will be held in secret US military prisons;<br />&nbsp; &nbsp;3. Gives US officials immunity from prosecution for torturing detainees that were captured before the end of 2005 by US military and CIA.</div><br />i haven&#039;t leant my support to any of that.<br /><br />in addition i&#039;ve got nothing but praise for what i know about Bayan USA and the affiliated organizations. i just think it&#039;s NAIVE to invest trust blindly.<br /><br />i&#039;m 16 and i go to stadium high school. our football team sucks but our facilities are ill. it really reminds me of the &quot;most baller shit in the world&quot; because it&#039;s largely fashion without function. but the misallocation of taxpayers&#039; dollars is another issue.<br /><br />&quot;Huh what are you trying to say??&nbsp; That because we agree with Geologic and other artists on this forum that we are somehow sucking up to them? that we perhaps DO NOT have a mind of our own?&quot;<br /><br />sorry what i said was brash. it wasn&#039;t targeted at everyone with a different opinion from myself, though. there are plenty of people who share your opinion who haven&#039;t been blessed by any massline artists.</div>
